<title>ROMANIA: Romanian leu closes weaker after quiet day.</title>
<headline>Romanian leu closes weaker after quiet day.</headline>
<dateline>BUCHAREST 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Romanian leu currency weakened to 6,850/7,100 to the dollar at Monday's close from about 6,700/7,000 in the morning after subdued trading, dealers said.</p>
<p>Money market traders said leu shortages still affected some banks, with overnight rates holding on 222/226 percent.</p>
<p>Quotes on banks' screens still reflected wide ranges, with some players practising huge spreads. Leu/dollar screen prices were between 6,200/7,000 and 6,900/8,400.</p>
<p>Leu/dollar retail prices hovered near 7,000/800.</p>
<p>-- Mirela Eremia, Bucharest Newsroom 40-1 3120264</p>
